CAT = "s66Funds"; SEG = "FND"
Q = [
('Shares of a closed-end fund are generally bought and sold:',
 'On an exchange at market price', ['Only by redemption at NAV', 'At NAV plus a sales charge', 'Directly from the sponsor daily'],
 'A closed-end fund issues a fixed number of shares that then trade like stock, often at a premium or discount to NAV. Redemption at NAV is how open-end mutual funds work.'),
('An ETF whose market price is above the value of its holdings is trading at a:',
 'Premium', ['Discount', 'Markup', 'Spread'],
 "When an ETF's market price exceeds its net asset value per share it trades at a premium; below NAV it trades at a discount. Creation and redemption by large firms usually keep the gap small."),
('A long-term investor placing a large sum with one fund family will usually pay least with:',
 'Class A shares at a breakpoint', ['Class C shares', 'Back-end load shares', 'Shares bought just under a breakpoint'],
 'Class A shares charge a front-end load that drops at breakpoints and carry lower yearly 12b-1 fees. Class C shares have higher ongoing fees, which cost more over many years.'),
('How does a unit investment trust differ from a mutual fund?',
 'Fixed, unmanaged portfolio', ['Shares trade only on exchanges', 'It has a portfolio manager', 'Units can never be redeemed'],
 'A UIT buys a set portfolio and holds it until the trust ends, with no ongoing management. UIT units are redeemable with the trust, so they are not locked in.'),
('Venture capital funds generally invest in:',
 'Early-stage private companies', ['Listed blue-chip stocks', 'Short-term Treasury bills', 'Investment-grade corporate bonds'],
 'Venture capital funds are private funds that buy stakes in young, private companies with high growth potential and high risk. Their holdings are illiquid and hard to value.'),
('A key risk of holding a digital asset in a self-hosted wallet is:',
 'Lost keys mean lost assets', ['FDIC limits on balances', 'SIPC claim delays', 'Daily NAV repricing'],
 'Whoever holds the private keys controls the asset, and there is generally no bank or custodian to restore access if the keys are lost. Digital assets are not FDIC insured.'),
("A client holds a fund that seeks twice the index's daily return for several months. The return may be:",
 'Far from twice the index', ['Exactly twice the index', 'Capped at the index return', 'Guaranteed above the index'],
 'Leveraged funds reset daily, so compounding over longer periods makes their results drift from the stated multiple, especially in a volatile market. They are built for short holding periods.'),
('Unlike an ETF, an exchange-traded note exposes the holder to:',
 'Issuer credit risk', ['Fund manager turnover', 'Underlying stock voting', 'Daily NAV redemption'],
 'An ETN is unsecured debt of the issuing bank that tracks an index. If the issuer fails, holders can lose money even if the index did well, whereas an ETF owns the underlying assets.'),
('A futures contract is best described as:',
 'Obligation to buy or sell later', ['Right, but no obligation, to buy', 'Loan backed by commodities', 'Share in a commodity pool'],
 'Both sides of a futures contract must perform at the set price on the delivery date unless they close out first. A right without an obligation describes an option buyer.'),
('The buyer of a put option has the right to:',
 'Sell at the strike price', ['Buy at the strike price', 'Collect the premium', 'Sell at the market price'],
 'A put gives its holder the right to sell the underlying at the strike price before expiration. The writer of the put collects the premium and must buy if assigned.'),
('Which annuity is a security that needs a securities license to sell?',
 'Variable annuity', ['Fixed annuity', 'Immediate fixed annuity', 'Fixed deferred annuity'],
 "A variable annuity's value depends on separate account investments, so it is a security. Fixed annuities, immediate or deferred, are insurance products with insurer-guaranteed payments."),
('Which type of life insurance builds no cash value?',
 'Term life', ['Whole life', 'Universal life', 'Variable life'],
 'Term insurance pays only a death benefit for a set period. Whole, universal and variable life are permanent policies that build cash value.'),
]
